WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.975
The patching sources are ISC's,
and the clock is CISA's.

2
00:00:03.975 --> 00:00:07.016
Subscribe to ISC's
bind-announce list and check

3
00:00:07.016 --> 00:00:10.212
its vulnerability matrix
for each version in use.

4
00:00:10.212 --> 00:00:15.702
And patch to CISA's clock: Binding
Operational Directive 26-04, from June 2026,

5
00:00:15.702 --> 00:00:20.763
replaced the older remediation
directives with risk-based timelines,

6
00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:26.338
the shortest three days for the highest-risk
flaws in publicly exposed assets.

7
00:00:26.338 --> 00:00:28.424
Version none hides the version.

8
00:00:28.424 --> 00:00:31.865
Query access defaults to
all hosts, so restrict it,

9
00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:35.138
and restrict recursion
to the agency's clients.

10
00:00:35.138 --> 00:00:39.476
Restrict zone transfers and
authenticate them with TSIG keys.

11
00:00:39.476 --> 00:00:44.200
Run named unprivileged, and
keep the host to DNS only.

12
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:51.174
For a baseline, CIS has benchmarks
only for BIND 9.11 and 9.9,

13
00:00:51.174 --> 00:00:53.400
none for 9.20 or 9.18.

14
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:59.210
So the agency states its own profile,
approved by the CISO, as design guidance.
